{
  "node_type": "statement",
  "body": {
    "id": "thm:gap-inference",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "statement": "Let \\(P\\) be a conditional-mean interior law in the published OVS model, and fix \\(n\\).  Suppose the observed-law derivative \\(D\\Delta_{\\mathrm{cmp},P}\\) in Definition \\(\\ref{def:gap-one-step}\\) is a well-defined linear functional on\n\\[\n\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}=\\{c't_{J_n,P}:c\\in\\mathbb R^{J_n}\\}\\subset L_2^0(P),\n\\]\nwhere \\(t_{J_n,P}\\) is projected against \\(Z_P^{\\mathrm{OVS}}\\).  Then every coordinate \\(t_{j,P}\\) belongs to \\(\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}\\),\n\\[\ng_{\\Delta,J_n,P}\\in\\operatorname{range}(G_{J_n,P}),\n\\]\nand\n\\[\n\\zeta_{\\Delta,J_n,P}=t_{J_n,P}'G_{J_n,P}^\\dagger g_{\\Delta,J_n,P}\n\\in\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}\\subseteq\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}\n\\]\nis the unique element of \\(\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}\\) satisfying\n\\[\nE_P[\\zeta_{\\Delta,J_n,P}s]=D\\Delta_{\\mathrm{cmp},P}[s]\n\\quad\\text{for every }s\\in\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}.\n\\]\nMoreover,\n\\[\nE_P[\\zeta_{\\Delta,J_n,P}^2]\n=g_{\\Delta,J_n,P}'G_{J_n,P}^\\dagger g_{\\Delta,J_n,P}.\n\\]\nThis is a population finite-sieve characterization in the published tangent space; it makes no growing-sieve or continuous-covariate Wald claim.",
    "free_symbols": [
      "P",
      "calM",
      "DeltaCmp",
      "tJ",
      "TangOVS",
      "Zovs",
      "zetaJ",
      "GJ",
      "gDelta",
      "Jseq",
      "n"
    ],
    "depends_on": [
      "def:gap-one-step",
      "lem:ovs-normal-tangent-projection"
    ],
    "proof_tex": "Fix \\(n\\), abbreviate \\(t=t_{J_n,P}\\), \\(G=E_P[tt']\\), \\(g=g_{\\Delta,J_n,P}\\), and \\(D=D\\Delta_{\\mathrm{cmp},P}\\).  Lemma \\(\\ref{lem:ovs-normal-tangent-projection}\\) gives\n\\[\nt_j=\\Pi_{\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}}\\{v_j-E_Pv_j\\}\n\\in\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}},\n\\qquad j=1,\\ldots,J_n.\n\\tag{G10}\n\\]\nTherefore \\(\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}=\\{c't:c\\in\\mathbb R^{J_n}\\}\\subseteq\\mathcal T_{P,\\mathrm{OVS}}\\).\n\nIf \\(c\\in\\ker G\\), then\n\\[\n0=c'Gc=E_P[(c't)^2],\n\\]\nso \\(c't=0\\) in \\(L_2(P)\\).  Linearity and well-definedness of \\(D\\) on \\(\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}\\) give\n\\[\nc'g=\\sum_{j=1}^{J_n}c_jD[t_j]=D[c't]=D[0]=0.\n\\tag{G11}\n\\]\nThus \\(g\\in(\\ker G)^\\perp=\\operatorname{range}G\\) and \\(GG^\\dagger g=g\\).\n\nPut \\(a=G^\\dagger g\\) and \\(\\zeta=t'a\\).  For \\(s=c't\\in\\mathcal S_{J_n,P}\\), symmetry of \\(G^\\dagger\\) and (G11) yield\n\\[\nE_P[\\zeta s]=a'Gc=g'G^\\dagger Gc=g'c=D[s].\n\\tag{G12}\n\\]\nIf \\(\\widetilde\\zeta\\) is another representer in the same space, use \\(s=\\widetilde\\zeta-\\zeta\\) in both representer identities to obtain\n\\(E_P[(\\widetilde\\zeta-\\zeta)^2]=0\\).  Hence the representer is unique in \\(L_2(P)\\).  Finally,\n\\[\nE_P[\\zeta^2]\n=g'G^\\dagger GG^\\dagger g=g'G^\\dagger g.\n\\]\nThis proves every population assertion; no step controls an estimated growing-dimensional Riesz map.",
    "justification": "The finite-sieve Riesz map is now constructed inside the published OVS tangent space.",
    "gap": "This population theorem deliberately leaves the continuous-covariate growing-sieve remainder outside its claim.",
    "consumer": "It supplies published-tangent coordinates for future general-covariate gap procedures.",
